40,"output_tokens":4415,"requests":7}}],"version":1},"findings":[{"block_threshold":0.8,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"Specify the helper's full vote-type -> label mapping (success->Verified+1, failure/cancelled->Verified-1) and add an AC proving the failure/cancelled path casts Verified -1.","cohort":["G6"],"criteria":["G6"],"decision":"block","decision_margin":0.0889,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["ADR 0023 Decision 1: sets `Verified +1` (CI passed) or `Verified -1` (failed/cancelled — fail-closed)","Workflow comment at gerrit-verify.yaml:513 'success -> Verified+1, failure|cancelled -> Verified-1 (fail-closed)'","normalize step vote-type domain is {clear,success,failure,cancelled} (gerrit-verify.yaml:455)","AC3 only asserts `Verified=1` for the success path; no AC covers the -1 negative vote"],"finding":"The helper's vote-value mapping is only specified/tested for the success case; the failure/cancelled -> `Verified -1` mapping mandated by ADR-0023 is neither specified in the Plan nor exercised by an AC.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fa76b4aed2356f7b9","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Plan: 'Result classification' / Acceptance Criteria AC3","norm_id":"n0e1a3b894ac5cea0","priority":0.8889,"reason":"high-priority+criterion-opted-in","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A failing/cancelled CI run reaches the final cast; the helper must set Verified -1 to keep the change unsubmittable, but only the +1 path is specified/tested"],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"State that the helper maps normalize's vote-type domain to Gerrit labels (success->+1, failure|cancelled->-1) and add a test asserting a `failure` vote-type sends `Verified=-1`.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.8889,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"yes","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"module","debt_impact":"medium","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"certification_cannot_prove","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"high","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.9,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Name and verify the exact `gerrit review` label-cast flag/value the helper emits (observe `gerrit review --help` or the Gerrit SSH docs — e.g. `--label Verified=+1` / legacy `--verified +1`), replace the AC's ambiguous `Verified=1` token with that literal, and pin it in test_success_vote_uses_the_verified_label_and_run_url.","cohort":["T3"],"criteria":["T3"],"decision":"block","decision_margin":0.1,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Plan: 'invoke Gerrit's documented SSH review command for the `Verified` label' and 'The run log ... reached `ssh ... gerrit review 2483,7 ...`' — the cited log is truncated BEFORE any label flag, so the flag is unobserved.","AC: 'proves the helper still sends `gerrit review <change>,<patchset>`, `Verified=1`' — `Verified=1` is not a valid gerrit-review argument by itself; the flag name is unspecified.","In-repo evidence: gerrit-verify.yaml:611-612 uses `gerrit review \"${CHANGE},${PS}\" --message ... --tag autogenerated:github`; infra/gerrit/reviewbot-e2e.sh:253 uses `gerrit review \"${CHANGE},${PS}\" --submit`. NO in-repo `gerrit review` call sets a label; label-cast is a NEW command surface.","ADR 0023 (:20-24) only says the action 'runs `gerrit review` to set Verified +1/-1' at the semantic level; it does not record the concrete flag syntax the new helper must emit.","Classification: Partially-verified — SSH transport/port/auth exist in-repo, but the specific label flag/value token is unconfirmed."],"finding":"The helper's `gerrit review` label-CAST flag is an asserted-but-unverified new CLI surface. Every existing in-repo `gerrit review` invocation sets only `--submit`, `--message`, or `--tag` — none sets a label — and the label-cast was previously encapsulated inside the opaque `gerrit-review-action`. The plan/AC describe the vote as `Verified=1` / `Verified +1`, but neither is a valid standalone `gerrit review` token; the actual command requires a flag (e.g. `--label Verified=+1` or legacy `--verified +1`) that the plan never names or verifies.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f7864e90147073c0e","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Plan section 'Result classification' / AC line 'test_success_vote_uses_the_verified_label_and_run_url' ('sends gerrit review <change>,<patchset>, Verified=1, port 29418')","norm_id":"n3b3efe5ae18db3ac","priority":1.0,"reason":"high-priority+criterion-opted-in","recalled":false,"scenarios":["Helper ships with a wrong or malformed label flag (e.g. `Verified=1` passed as a bare arg, or `--verified` on a Gerrit build that only accepts `--label`), the SSH command exits nonzero at runtime, and the fail-closed path reddens CI on EVERY successful build — the opposite of the bug being fixed.","A test mock asserts the truncated `Verified=1` string that the plan wrote, so the suite passes green while the real Gerrit rejects the flag in production."],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":1.0,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"yes","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"yes","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"module","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"certification_cannot_prove","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"high","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"high"}}},{"block_threshold":0.95,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Add a step/AC to record the new closed-change=successful-noop disposition in ADR 0023 (or a linked doc) so the documented Verified-gate contract matches the helper's behavior.","cohort":["COH","E1","E2","E6","F1","T2","T4","T5e","T7"],"criteria":["T7","T5e"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":0.05,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Plan cites 'ADR 0023 defines the inbound path as SSH gerrit review setting Verified +1 for success or Verified -1 for failed/cancelled'","Plan adds a new terminal disposition ('exit 0 because the change has already moved to a terminal unvoteable state') not reflected in that ADR","ABSENCE: no acceptance criterion or step updates ADR 0023 or any doc to record the closed-change=noop disposition"],"finding":"The plan introduces a new behavioral rule — a Gerrit 'fatal: change is closed' response is recorded as a successful (Verified vote skipped, exit 0) disposition — that is not captured in any doc/ADR, even though it cites ADR 0023 as the authority for the inbound Verified-vote path.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f4504bf03631d62cb","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Plan section 'Plan' / 'Root cause'","norm_id":"ne1bab6332d44e01b","priority":1.0,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A future maintainer reads ADR 0023, sees only +1/-1 dispositions, and is surprised that closed-change races silently pass CI without a Verified vote"],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"Add a short note to ADR 0023 documenting that a 'fatal: change is closed' Gerrit response is treated as a benign superseded disposition (no Verified vote, non-failing), and reference the new scripts/cast_gerrit_verified_vote.py helper.","tier":"LLM","validity":1.0,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"na","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"medium","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"uncertifiable_outcome","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"none","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":null,"blocking_enabled":null,"checklist_item":"","cohort":null,"criteria":["P6"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":null,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["2 criterion line(s) bundle multiple deliverables with 'and' (split so each is independently verifiable)."],"finding":"Acceptance-criteria / definition-of-done quality issues.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f607dd457c67f9209","impact":0.4,"is_primary":null,"location":"","norm_id":"ned06ebc801a522e3","priority":0.4,"reason":null,"recalled":false,"scenarios":[],"severity":"minor","suggested_fix":"Split compound criteria, replace subjective terms with observable outcomes, and state how each is